steps.instructions:
Practice data modification:

```sql
-- Update a student's marks
UPDATE marks SET marks = 90 WHERE student_id = 1 AND subject = 'Computer';

-- Verify the update
SELECT s.name, m.subject, m.marks
FROM students s JOIN marks m ON s.id = m.student_id
WHERE s.id = 1;

-- Delete a student (first remove related marks)
DELETE FROM marks WHERE student_id = 5;
DELETE FROM students WHERE id = 5;

-- Add a new column
ALTER TABLE students ADD COLUMN batch TEXT DEFAULT '2026-A';

-- Update batch for some students
UPDATE students SET batch = '2026-B' WHERE city = 'Delhi';

-- Create an index for faster searches
CREATE INDEX idx_student_email ON students(email);
CREATE INDEX idx_marks_student ON marks(student_id);

-- Check indexes
SELECT * FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'index';
```

Verify:
- After UPDATE, marks changed for student 1
- After DELETE, student 5 and their marks are gone
- New `batch` column exists in the students table
- Indexes are listed in sqlite_master

Save all queries to your `.sql` file.
